#: data/io.github.moooossee.Moose.metainfo.xml.in
msgid ""
"Ask questions, work on your writing or get help with code. Chat with AI "
"running on your computer through Ollama, or use an online service such as "
"OpenRouter with your own key. Browse models for the things you want to do, "
"or download compatible models from Hugging Face."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.moooossee.Moose.metainfo.xml.in
msgid ""
"Bring photos, PDFs and text files into the conversation. Your attachments "
"and the documents you create are together in Files, where you can preview "
"them, search your library and return to a related chat. Answers can show "
"passages from your documents so you can check where information came from. "
"Pictures need a model that can understand them, and PDFs need text you can "
"select."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.moooossee.Moose.metainfo.xml.in
msgid ""
"Ask Moose to write a report, put together a budget or prepare a "
"presentation. Describe what you need or use an answer you already have, then "
"choose PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OpenDocument or a text or data format. "
"Your documents stay with the answer, so you can preview them, open them in "
"another application or save a copy whenever you need."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.moooossee.Moose.metainfo.xml.in
msgid ""
"Edit a message, try a different answer or go back to an earlier version. If "
"an answer reaches its limit, you can ask it to continue. Drafts save as you "
"go, and code and math are formatted to make them easier to read."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.moooossee.Moose.metainfo.xml.in
msgid ""
"When you want to look something up or check a calculation, turn on Web or "
"Calculator with a compatible Ollama or Ollama Cloud model. You can read the "
"sources and see what the tools did alongside the answer."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.moooossee.Moose.metainfo.xml.in
msgid ""
"Your chats, drafts and document library are saved on your device. You decide "
"whether messages or files can be shared with an online service, with "
"separate permissions you can reset in Privacy settings. Web asks for its own "
"permission: search services receive your searches, websites receive requests "
"for the pages you read, and results are shared with the model answering your "
"chat. Each service's privacy policy applies to what you share. Local Only "
"uses only Ollama managed by Moose and turns off web tools. Keys for online "
"services are kept in your desktop's secure key storage."
msgstr ""

